WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue { font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; background: #000000; }
::cue(.narrator) { color: #FFFF00; }

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.100 line:85% align:center
GENTLE PIANO MUSIC

2
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.286 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>Every child is born
curious about sound.</c>

3
00:00:04.286 --> 00:00:09.323 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>In China, more and more parents want
their children to start music early.</c>

4
00:00:09.323 --> 00:00:11.441 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>But there is little
professional guidance,</c>

5
00:00:11.441 --> 00:00:14.286 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>and few products made
for young children.</c>

6
00:00:14.286 --> 00:00:17.172 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>Real instruments
can feel too hard...</c>

7
00:00:17.172 --> 00:00:20.000 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>...and most music toys, too simple.</c>

8
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.186 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>Yet ages three to six
are a golden window.</c>

9
00:00:23.186 --> 00:00:25.309 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>Children can follow
rhythm and melody,</c>

10
00:00:25.309 --> 00:00:28.571 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>and they learn best through play.</c>

11
00:00:28.571 --> 00:00:31.274 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>So I interviewed twelve people.</c>

12
00:00:31.274 --> 00:00:35.714 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>Music educators, early-childhood
teachers, and parents.</c>

13
00:00:35.714 --> 00:00:38.538 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>One mother told me:
"I've never learned music.</c>

14
00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:42.857 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>I want it to guide me,
without restricting my child."</c>

15
00:00:42.857 --> 00:00:48.571 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>The key insight? Emotional expression
matters more than technical skill.</c>

16
00:00:48.571 --> 00:00:54.286 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>Meet Melody Mate. A music toy
for children aged three to six.</c>

17
00:00:54.286 --> 00:01:00.000 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>Nine instrument tokens.
Each with its own voice.</c>

18
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.286 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>Place one on the toy,
and it begins to play.</c>

19
00:01:04.286 --> 00:01:06.756 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>Soft touch zones move
with the rhythm,</c>

20
00:01:06.756 --> 00:01:10.000 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>so children can feel the music.</c>

21
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.000 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>A friendly guide leads the way,
through Create, Learn, and Challenge.</c>

22
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.582 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>In testing, children
missed the touch area,</c>

23
00:01:17.582 --> 00:01:21.429 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>and needed more help
in Challenge mode.</c>

24
00:01:21.429 --> 00:01:26.429 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>So now, the guide leads every step,
from start to finish.</c>

25
00:01:26.429 --> 00:01:30.248 line:85% align:center
<c.narrator>Melody Mate.
Music you can touch.</c>

